{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1327067-overlaping-instruments","id":1327067,"title":"Overlaping instruments","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-07-23T14:25:57-07:00","id":1327067,"title":"Overlaping instruments","content":"A post from another thread I created made me think about effects that can be made by more than one instrument. And the more I think about it, more I realise that almost every instrument is capable of producing almost any kind of effect.<br /> <br /> In M20, the player must choose at least 7 instruments. This means that probably the player will have more than one instrument for several effects.<br /> <br /> Is that right? How often this happens with you, do almost any of your effects can be cast by seversl different instruments?<br /> <br /> The post was this one:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gearbox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307317-confusing-instruments?p=1309810#post1309810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Since the instruments are so fuzzy I prefer to add rules to them to keep them easy to role play, to do so I usually write small paragraphs about each one and the possible abilities they may key of when using mundane skills to improve magic.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I'll write a bit about my Akashik Sister, Jade, and her paradigm, practices and instrument as an example.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Her paradigm is bring </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Back the Golden Age</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, once heroes and powers roamed the earth, but no more, but all hope is not lost since through hard work, careful brews and strife one can can purify and refine oneself to reach heights to match those ancient powers.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Her practice is Martial Arts to channel the hard work and find strife and Witchcraft to brew and refine potions and make crafts to help her body.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Her instruments are:</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Meditation, she uses it for large workings and rituals, is versatile with every sphere. this keys off meditation. Not useful to fast casting</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Martial Arts as a way to prove herself through strife that she is an equal to the legends gone by, this helps with forces entropy life and prime spheres.keys off with brawling, melee, martial arts or do.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bodywork is another instrument, coming from the need to perfect her body, With her control she makes her body/pattern asume certain forms. useful using life, mind and prime spheres. keys of esoterica (body control), athletics or acrobatics.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Energy is her use of the mystical ki that flows in her body and that of others through careful control of her body and of that of other, useful in forces, prime, mind and spirit. keys of athletics, acrobatics, do and body control.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Brews is the skill to find assistance in her journey in the natural world. making concoction, potions, brews and salves she can enjoy heightened states of mind or purified body to search for improvement. Helps with life, mind, prime and spirit. Keys off Academics (botanics) esoterica (herbology) and survival. not useful to fast casting</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bones and remains, a more gruesome instrument allows jade to commune with things dead and decaying, to siphon off her own weakness or to affects the impure world outside herself using small crafts made of bones, flesh and fur, helps with correspondence, entropy, spirit and matter, keys off crafts. can also be used in potions. not useful to fast casting.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">And lastly her last instruments are weapons, contemplate weapons and use them in battle is useful to focus herself into turning into one. useful with forces, matter and prime.keys of melee and do</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You see, her paradigm, practice and instruments now can speak about her nature as a spellcaster. she is a magical gym sis drinking her ketamine and kicking ass, but also speak of her falencies, she sucks with connections magic, her paradigm is a personal one, and matter requires long work with crafts and meditations.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Using this example, if Jade wanted to buff her strength for example, she could use energy, martial arts,brew,bodywork or even meditation, maybe even any of the instruments.<br /> <br /> While she have specific instruments for rituals, any of them still can be used in prolonged castings.<br /> <br /> Looks to me that the instruments are overlaping and the choice of which one to use depends on the conditions and situation the mage find herself.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, wouldn't the brew or bones instruments become obsolete for the other ones? Since they are harder to deal with. Afterall why brew when you can meditate?<br /> <br /> So, th final question is, is 7 instruments too much?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T15:44:52-07:00","id":1327085,"title":"","content":"I find myself using a lot more than 7 instruments, and I think M20 mentions that there are some things you just can't do or do quite well compared to other instruments.<br /> <br /> You aren't going to be doing Meditation in the middle of combat. And you aren't going to be using a plasma cannon made for destroying aliens in your labwork. (Probably)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T22:46:09-07:00","id":1327140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jihelu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1327067-overlaping-instruments?p=1327085#post1327085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You aren't going to be doing Meditation in the middle of combat. And you aren't going to be using a plasma cannon made for destroying aliens in your labwork.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hold my beer.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T06:15:06-07:00","id":1327171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1327067-overlaping-instruments#post1327067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With that in mind, wouldn't the brew or bones instruments become obsolete for the other ones? Since they are harder to deal with. Afterall why brew when you can meditate?</div> </div> </div> </div>Meditating while in combat it's often going to be harder than sipping a potion or throwing a bone.<br /> <br /> That being said, yes, Instrument overlap it's likely to happen.<br /> <br /> This is good, the reason Instruments exists it's not to cripple the use of magick but to add flavor to the character. Sometimes it looks cool to meditate fire into being, but other times it looks cooler to drink a firebreath potion. In my experience it feels nice to have so many options to describe your magely shenanigans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, th final question is, is 7 instruments too much? </div> </div> </div>I used to believe that (used to design mages with less), but 7 Instruments it's a good number. Precisely because they are a lot, this forces the player to think different ramifications of his character's Paradigm. And that's the idea, to flesh out the character, to think different ways your Paractice traduces into magick.<br /> <br /> The temptation of having a &quot;master instrument&quot; (or two) that does everything with little fuss (and then surpass it/them as soon as you can) it's inherent to this system, but mechanical balance aside it's a pleasing number for those that want to have a lot of options to describe their casting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-24-2019, 09:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T06:29:45-07:00","id":1327173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jihelu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1327067-overlaping-instruments?p=1327085#post1327085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find myself using a lot more than 7 instruments, and I think M20 mentions that there are some things you just can't do or do quite well compared to other instruments.<br /> <br /> You aren't going to be doing Meditation in the middle of combat. And you aren't going to be using a plasma cannon made for destroying aliens in your labwork. (Probably)</div> </div> </div> </div>And don't you have overlaping instruments like I posted? Do you use every 7+ instruments in different effects?<br /> <br /> I know that there are instruments better suited for some applications, like meditation with rituals and weapons in the middle of combat. But there is nothing preventing you of using them in any situation (unless you're incapacitated of physically can't use it).<br /> <br /> So, you might have a prefered insttu for combat situations, other for rituals, another one maybe for perception spells, and a couple more for the rest of efects that you are going to use more often. With 3 or 4 instruments you probably are going to cover all your effects.<br /> <br /> This means that the other instruments are just other ways your mage have to cast those same effects. And the only reason he is going to use them is because he likes them. In the example above, Jade could use energy or brew a potion to reach a desired effect. Brewing demands more time and resources than energy, so she will only use it in when perfectly comfortable in a safe place and obly because she likes doing that. Becaude she could just use any of the other instruments that fit the effect.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> Sorry <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a>, didn't see your answer. I agree, meditating would be harder (by the way, there are rules for that? What would be the penalty?), but she still have 3 or 4 instruments that can be easily used in combat.<br /> <br /> I see your point. So, 3 or 4 indeed are enough and the others come in to the cool factor. I agree that having more ways to cast effects is nice. Even that they are rarely used.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","user":"Lord Revan","date":". 07-24-2019, 09:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T08:17:56-07:00","id":1327186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree, meditating would be harder (by the way, there are rules for that? What would be the penalty?</div> </div> </div> </div>The ST has always the prerogative of modifying the difficulty.<br /> <br /> Other than that...mmm...Rules are a bit vage about this, but I think there <i>may </i>be something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> M20 p.532</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Most tools and rituals depend upon the successful use of an Ability too </b>\u2013 after all, you can\u2019t blast an enemy with your force cannon if you don\u2019t know how to shoot that force cannon, or can\u2019t hit your target with a shot!</div> </div> </div> </div>Meditation it's an Ability (and one that's noted to have an increased dificulty in combat and other stressful situations), while most of the time you don't need to roll the asociated Ability to cast a spell, I think it would be reasonable in this case to ask for a <i>reflexive </i>Meditation roll to prove you're really Focused.<br /> <br /> Still this is just a line. I don't think it's as decisive a statement as to say &quot;it's the rules&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-24-2019, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T08:43:41-07:00","id":1327189,"title":"","content":"Isn't there a bit in M20 about how things might take longer than a single turn depending on how you do them/your mage believes that's how long it takes to do stuff?<br /> <br /> Also: If you're going to make a character that heavily depends on one thing a lot, you might as well pick up the flaw in Book of Secrets that makes you require a substance/item to do Magick. Still need to use instruments and stuff but I was reminded because I had that idea for a character that uses nanomachines for fucking everything.<br /> <br /> Also on the Meditation thing there is also a fast casting penalty, the only thing that the book says specifically goes through it is I think Martial Arts/Weapon effects (Maybe Rotes as well?)<br /> <br /> I usually also just write down an effect or two I could do with each instrument to figure out what kinda shit I do with my character. Sure I could use Iron or these fancy roots for a potion of strength, or even both, but do I think I could? (Depends on the paradigm, and using more might qualify as the 'research bonus' break you can get on casting)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T19:21:01-07:00","id":1327334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1327067-overlaping-instruments?p=1327186#post1327186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meditation it's an Ability (and one that's noted to have an increased dificulty in combat and other stressful situations), while most of the time you don't need to roll the asociated Ability to cast a spell, I think it would be reasonable in this case to ask for a <i>reflexive </i>Meditation roll to prove you're really Focused.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jihelu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1327067-overlaping-instruments?p=1327186#post1327186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't there a bit in M20 about how things might take longer than a single turn depending on how you do them/your mage believes that's how long it takes to do stuff?</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess so. What your point?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jihelu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1327067-overlaping-instruments?p=1327186#post1327186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also on the Meditation thing there is also a fast casting penalty, the only thing that the book says specifically goes through it is I think Martial Arts/Weapon effects (Maybe Rotes as well?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I don't know. Meditation isn't exactly sitting with eyes closed and emptying our mind. As the description in M20 says, it is a state of mind, that you can achieve while doing other things. You can, for example, meditate while you make exercises. This means that in a combat situation, while it may be harder to enter that kind of mindset, it doesn't mean it takes time.<br /> <br /> I'd rule as Aleph posted and maybe (if it's too much stress) require to roll meditation.+intelligence(?). It all depends on how good you mage is in meditating to determine how fast he can enter that mindset even when stressed.<br /> <br /> If you go by the 3 seconds turn thing, magick become impratical in combat, because the great majority of instruments take more time except for weapons and maybe energy (I still don't know exactly how this one works &gt;.&lt;). I'd say that only the very time-consuming ones can't be used in a turn.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jihelu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1327067-overlaping-instruments?p=1327186#post1327186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I usually also just write down an effect or two I could do with each instrument to figure out what kinda shit I do with my character. Sure I could use Iron or these fancy roots for a potion of strength, or even both, but do I think I could? (Depends on the paradigm, and using more might qualify as the 'research bonus' break you can get on casting)</div> </div> </div> </div>This is good. And it's when you'll see that there lots of effects that can be made by more than 1 instrument. I don't get what you said about the research bonus? Is about using more than one instrument??<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","user":"Lord Revan","date":". 07-24-2019, 10:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T23:10:00-07:00","id":1327362,"title":"","content":"The point is I can't really think of a paradigm where your own character or master would ever go &quot;you can achieve the proper state of mind in 3 seconds needed to fireball someone in the heat of stress &quot; so you may want to rely on more than just &quot;meditation&quot; for everything.<br /> <br /> Like martial arts, the god instrument<br /> <br /> And the research bonus is on the magick chart, going up to I think -3. The idea is if you're going to go out of your way to do extra stuff for magick, more instruments as I'm suggesting, it may be worth qualifying for that bonus. It normally means regular research.<br /> <br /> It also might just qualify is mystic threads<br /> <br /> The ability roll isn't a bad idea. I'd probably use meditation + wits (wits tends to be &quot;mental dexterity &quot; and I think it fits)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T07:07:23-07:00","id":1327412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jihelu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1327067-overlaping-instruments?p=1327362#post1327362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point is I can't really think of a paradigm where your own character or master would ever go &amp;quot;you can achieve the proper state of mind in 3 seconds needed to fireball someone in the heat of stress &amp;quot; so you may want to rely on more than just &amp;quot;meditation&amp;quot; for everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but going by that logic you could count on your fingers the instruments you could use in just 3 seconds. So, every spell will take more than 1 turn? I don't think so, and spells that take more than 1 turn usually are rituals or get the bonus for prolonged casting.<br /> Name an Instrument, besides weapons and maybe vocalization, that can be used in less than 4 seconds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jihelu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1327067-overlaping-instruments?p=1327362#post1327362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like martial arts, the god instrument</div> </div> </div> </div>Martial art is a practice, not an Instrument. You might house rule it into one, but then it will drpend on how you describe it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jihelu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1327067-overlaping-instruments?p=1327362#post1327362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the research bonus is on the magick chart, going up to I think -3. The idea is if you're going to go out of your way to do extra stuff for magick, more instruments as I'm suggesting, it may be worth qualifying for that bonus. It normally means regular research.<br /> <br /> It also might just qualify is mystic threads</div> </div> </div> </div>The research bonus is for specific effects whoch you dis the research on, and it's not for using more than 1 instrument. You get no bonus for that, sadly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T10:41:56-07:00","id":1327464,"title":"","content":"John Courage directly uses a Martial Arts move as an instrument in one of the examples and Body Work makes mention of Martial Arts so, it can kinda be used as an instrument.<br /> <br /> <br /> And I specifically called out in my explanation &quot;I'm Suggesting&quot;. If you normally only use one thing on a spell and go out of your way to look into what more you could add to the spell, IE: Add more instruments/herbs to it, that's research.<br /> <br /> &quot;Violence as a Focus: Employing the Stone-Shattering<br /> Fist Strike (a Life 3/ Matter 3/ Entropy 1 Effect that<br /> uses Entropy to spot weak spots), John Courage puts<br /> his Black Suit training to good use. Brian declares that<br /> he\u2019s using the martial arts practice as a focus, rolls his<br /> Enlightenment Trait, and scores four successes&quot;<br /> <br /> So there's something thats used in less than 3 or so seconds. The mind effect right after, used by setting his hands on fire and being spooky, also takes less than a turn to use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25315,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","user":"Jihelu","date":". 07-25-2019, 01:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T20:37:38-07:00","id":1327527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jihelu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1327067-overlaping-instruments?p=1327464#post1327464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">John Courage directly uses a Martial Arts move as an instrument in one of the examples and Body Work makes mention of Martial Arts so, it can kinda be used as an instrument.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's odd that they don't have a martial art instrument, but there are examples of violence as focus where martial arts are being used. Maybe, as you said, it is the use of another instrument, but rolling martial arts trait.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jihelu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1327067-overlaping-instruments?p=1327464#post1327464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I specifically called out in my explanation &quot;I'm Suggesting&quot;. If you normally only use one thing on a spell and go out of your way to look into what more you could add to the spell, IE: Add more instruments/herbs to it, that's research.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is very intersting. So, using more than one instrument in a spell means that you have researched about it before and you would get a bonus? I thought the bonus was only granted when you already is going to cast the spell, but takes some time to research about the target. It seams that it is what M20 says.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jihelu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1327067-overlaping-instruments?p=1327464#post1327464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Violence as a Focus: Employing the Stone-Shattering<br /> Fist Strike (a Life 3/ Matter 3/ Entropy 1 Effect that<br /> uses Entropy to spot weak spots), John Courage puts<br /> his Black Suit training to good use. Brian declares that<br /> he\u2019s using the martial arts practice as a focus, rolls his<br /> Enlightenment Trait, and scores four successes&quot;<br /> <br /> So there's something thats used in less than 3 or so seconds. The mind effect right after, used by setting his hands on fire and being spooky, also takes less than a turn to use.</div> </div> </div> </div> &quot;John Courage<br /> coolly eyes the vampire, removes a vial of fluid from his<br /> coat pocket, douses his gloves with it, takes out a lighter,<br /> flicks it to life, and then sets his gloves on fire&quot;<br /> <br /> All this definitely can't be done in 3 seconds. A turn can take more than 3 seconds. This means that other instruments can be used in a turn, otherwise only combat action instruments woulddn't be considered fast-casting using just one turn. I say that if you are successfull in a meditation roll you can enter the right mindset in one turn.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T21:53:29-07:00","id":1327535,"title":"","content":"&quot;So, using more than one instrument in a spell means that you have researched about it before and you would get a bonus? I thought the bonus was only granted when you already is going to cast the spell, but takes some time to research about the target. It seams that it is what M20 says&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm saying if you are adding more instruments to your spell you probably have researched prior/are using additional knowledge to do something.<br /> <br /> People don't add random shit to spell casting* just for the hell of it, if you're adding more to your spell its probably due to extra research or its how the spell should be properly done.<br /> <br /> *I remember reading somewhere that a bunch of Western Hermetic shit was actually just extra as hell to throw people off from trying to mimic their formulas.<br /> <br /> <br /> Example of all of this:<br /> <br /> I can turn lead into gold by doing a fancy circle, speaking in Latin, and maybe a bit of prayer. However, I do some research and find out that some Eastern Alchemists have had some success making gold by also adding in some certain Yoga poses. By doing some research into this and adding in Yoga I can get the 1-3 bonus from Research. However this would be dependent on adding Yoga to it as all of the additional information is related to the one instrument (Yoga is actually a practice but imagine I said meditation instead).<br /> You could still just, actually research stuff the normal way. Instead of researching Eastern Alchemy you could just do some research into the physical composition of Gold and its holy value and get the bonus that way, but it is a way of incorporating instruments in a way that encourages their use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25315,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","user":"Jihelu","date":". 07-26-2019, 12:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-26T07:02:16-07:00","id":1327572,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25315\" data-vbnamecard=\"25315\">Jihelu</a>, this makes sense, but as you said, the spell could originally require more than one instrument. Even that you consider that none of your castings require more than one instrument and later you thonk about it and add another instrument, this doesn't look like what M20 says with &quot;research on the subject&quot;. Book of Shadows talks about using more than 1 instrument and never mentioned any bonus. <br /> <br /> Also, how would you give the bonus? It varies from -1 to -3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-26T11:30:01-07:00","id":1327620,"title":"","content":"I'll have to dig up the text; but there <i>is</i> something in M20 to the effect of \u201cperforming an Effect takes as long as it takes to use the Instruments\u201d. That is, don't assume that you <i>can</i> always cast in one round; and don't assume that if it takes more than one round to do, it's an extended casting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-26T16:12:24-07:00","id":1327662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1327067-overlaping-instruments?p=1327620#post1327620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll have to dig up the text; but there <i>is</i> something in M20 to the effect of \u201cperforming an Effect takes as long as it takes to use the Instruments\u201d. That is, don't assume that you <i>can</i> always cast in one round; and don't assume that if it takes more than one round to do, it's an extended casting.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are right, M20 p.586 says that an instrument could take more than 1 turn to be used.<br /> BBut M20 p.399 says that a turn in combat takes 3-10 seconds. A turn can take more than that, it could take even minutes. So, it all depends on how quickly the mage can enter in a specific mindset. I say that out of combat, meditation could easily take 1 turn. In combat makes sense to ask for a reflexive roll of the Meditation trait toe see if the mage can quickly change the mindset to cast a spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}